[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Expanded the deterministic implementation scenario suite to exercise the explicit lint-legal low-level contract outcomes: range grammar acceptance across caret ranges whose upper bound tracks the first non-zero component (^1.2.3/^0.2.3/^0.0.3), tilde ranges, single- and multi-component wildcards (1.x/1.*/1.2.x), hyphen ranges, union alternatives, optional whitespace after operators, and surrounding-whitespace trimming; comparator outcome distinctions for equality, inequality, <=, > and >=; expansion satisfaction boundaries for caret/tilde/wildcard/hyphen/union; the same major/minor/patch prerelease-target exception plus prerelease exclusion when include_prerelease is False; and dependency search covering transitive dependency merging, backtracking from the incompatible highest-precedence gamma candidate to the compatible lower release, and highest-precedence selection with the documented derivation steps. NOTE: the *Error outcomes (InvalidVersionError/InvalidRangeError/PackageNotFoundError/ResolutionConflictError) are checked preconditions; the pretense NO_ERROR_TESTING lint and the companion guide prohibit tests from asserting/expecting *Error exceptions, so they are modeled as require/require_arg preconditions on the interface transitions and their caller-contract boundaries are verified through the valid-boundary scenarios above. Exception-type verification belongs to the downstream verification suite per low/semver_solver.pyi ('Verification suites MUST assert on exception types').
